[thin] Wrong material-thickness classification at an inside pocket corner: each pair joins the world-vertical support exit's fore face (Y19.132) to the seating-floor vertex where the inset's R6.15 lower round crosses the exit's inboard plane |X|62.65; the normals are exactly 120° apart and the material between is the inset's solid corner surround. Rays from the pair cross 9.1 mm and 6.2 mm of material (probe on the current STL). The real section here is the 1.80 mm wing-retention lip (3.84 - 1.44 - 0.60), which the accepted face-up cover needs: display-cover/face-up-trial records its 3.30 mm capture and the receiver passed the 2026-09-30 shake test.
alternatives: A thicker lip needs a deeper inset (cover below flush), thinner wings or less wing air, each a change to the accepted fit; the exits stay world-vertical so supports leave into the display storey.
