[sliver] Required by the purchased K&J SB443-IN's side grooves: each magnet column's slot in the receiver wall is the printed capture Derek specified for these stepped blocks, faces touching, loaded at one print pause. The 1.575 mm faces seat each block's 1.6 mm front band from the bay face to its rails, the 1.500 mm faces are the rails' tips standing in the 1.6 mm grooves, and the 0.797 mm faces are the rails' fore and aft bearing faces. Each runs the slot's 26 mm. pump-dock/magnet-retention.md gives the slot.
alternatives: A wider or deeper rail does not enter the 1.6 × 0.79 mm groove. A cover across the pole face separates the required touching poles. The specified groove-bearing interface requires this local section.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-top.step
